<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.4.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan"
              testname="Poll Answering — Participant Vote Load Test" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Load test for the participant "poll answering" path.

WHAT IT DOES
  1. SETUP  (1 thread) — creates a 4-option poll draft and STARTs it, so votes are accepted.
  2. PARTICIPANTS (${NUM_PARTICIPANTS} threads, ramped over ${RAMP_UP_SEC}s) — each virtual
     participant casts VOTES_PER_PARTICIPANT votes (re-voting is realistic: votes are mutable),
     each vote picking a random option 0..${MAX_OPTION_INDEX}.
       POST ${VOTE_PATH}
       Header:  X-Participant-ID: &lt;stable per-thread UUID&gt;
       Body:    {"options":[&lt;random idx&gt;]}
       Expect:  HTTP 204
  3. TEARDOWN (1 thread) — clears the poll.

DEFAULT TARGET = the LOCAL DAEMON (http://127.0.0.1:1234), which needs no auth and is the safe
default (it does NOT hammer production). The daemon serves ONE session, so the participant vote
path has no /{session_id} prefix and the host path's session segment is a throw-away placeholder.

  ⚠ This mutates LIVE poll state on the target daemon (switches activity to "poll", broadcasts to
    any connected participants). Run it against an idle/non-live daemon. Teardown clears it.

TO POINT AT PRODUCTION (https://interact.victorrentea.ro) edit the User Defined Variables,
substituting the active session id into the two paths:
  PROTOCOL       = https
  HOST           = interact.victorrentea.ro
  PORT           = 443
  VOTE_PATH      = /&lt;session_id&gt;/api/participant/poll/vote      (prod needs the session prefix)
  HOST_POLL_BASE = /api/&lt;session_id&gt;/host/poll
  AUTH_USER / AUTH_PASS = host-panel credentials (~/.training-assistants-secrets.env)
(Host endpoints are Basic-Auth protected on prod; the AuthManager below supplies the
credentials. On localhost the credentials are simply unused.)

No plugins required — pure HTTP samplers.</stringProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.functional_mode">false</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.tearDown_on_shutdown">true</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.serialize_threadgroups">false</boolProp>
      <elementProp name="TestPlan.user_defined_variables" elementType="Arguments"
                   guiclass="ArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments"
                   testname="User Defined Variables" enabled="true">
        <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
          <!-- ── Connection (defaults = local daemon) ─────────── -->
          <elementProp name="PROTOCOL" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">PROTOCOL</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">http</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="HOST" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">HOST</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">127.0.0.1</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="PORT" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">PORT</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">1234</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <!-- ── Paths (daemon-direct defaults) ───────────────── -->
          <elementProp name="VOTE_PATH" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">VOTE_PATH</stringProp>
            <!-- Daemon-direct: /api/participant/poll/vote
                 Prod:          /&lt;session_id&gt;/api/participant/poll/vote  (put the real session id in the path) -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">/api/participant/poll/vote</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="HOST_POLL_BASE" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">HOST_POLL_BASE</stringProp>
            <!-- Base for host poll draft/start/clear. "loadtest" is a throw-away session segment
                 for the daemon (which serves one session). Prod: /api/&lt;session_id&gt;/host/poll -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">/api/loadtest/host/poll</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <!-- ── Auth (used only against production host endpoints) ─ -->
          <elementProp name="AUTH_USER" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">AUTH_USER</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">CHANGE_ME</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="AUTH_PASS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">AUTH_PASS</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">CHANGE_ME</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <!-- ── Poll shape ───────────────────────────────────── -->
          <elementProp name="MULTI" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">MULTI</stringProp>
            <!-- false = single-choice poll (each vote sends exactly one option) -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">false</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="MAX_OPTION_INDEX" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">MAX_OPTION_INDEX</stringProp>
            <!-- Highest valid 0-based option index. The setup poll has 4 options → 3.
                 If you change the option count in the setup draft, update this too. -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">3</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <!-- ── Load profile ─────────────────────────────────── -->
          <elementProp name="NUM_PARTICIPANTS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">NUM_PARTICIPANTS</stringProp>
            <!-- Concurrent virtual participants -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">200</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="RAMP_UP_SEC" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">RAMP_UP_SEC</stringProp>
            <!-- Seconds to start all participant threads -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">20</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="VOTES_PER_PARTICIPANT" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">VOTES_PER_PARTICIPANT</stringProp>
            <!-- Votes (incl. re-votes) each participant casts. Total requests = NUM_PARTICIPANTS × this. -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">5</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="VOTE_INTERVAL_MS" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">VOTE_INTERVAL_MS</stringProp>
            <!-- Pause between a participant's successive votes. Set 0 for max-throughput stress. -->
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">800</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
        </collectionProp>
      </elementProp>
    </TestPlan>
    <hashTree>

      <!-- Applies HOST/PORT/PROTOCOL to every HTTP sampler below -->
      <ConfigTestElement guiclass="HttpDefaultsGui" testclass="ConfigTestElement"
                         testname="HTTP Request Defaults (${PROTOCOL}://${HOST}:${PORT})" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.domain">${HOST}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.port">${PORT}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.protocol">${PROTOCOL}</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.follow_redirects">true</boolProp>
        <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.use_keepalive">true</boolProp>
        <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments">
          <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments"/>
        </elementProp>
      </ConfigTestElement>
      <hashTree/>

      <!-- Basic Auth — needed only for prod host endpoints; unused on localhost -->
      <AuthManager guiclass="AuthPanel" testclass="AuthManager"
                   testname="HTTP Basic Auth (host endpoints)" enabled="true">
        <collectionProp name="AuthManager.auth_list">
          <elementProp name="" elementType="Authorization">
            <stringProp name="Authorization.url">${PROTOCOL}://${HOST}:${PORT}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Authorization.username">${AUTH_USER}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Authorization.password">${AUTH_PASS}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Authorization.domain"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Authorization.realm"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Authorization.mechanism">BASIC</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
        </collectionProp>
      </AuthManager>
      <hashTree/>

      <!-- ================================================================
           1. SETUP: create a 4-option poll draft, then start it
           ================================================================ -->
      <SetupThreadGroup guiclass="SetupThreadGroupGui" testclass="SetupThreadGroup"
                        testname="Setup: Create and Start Poll" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">stoptest</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController"
                     guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController">
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">false</boolProp>
          <stringProp name="LoopController.loops">1</stringProp>
        </elementProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">1</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">0</stringProp>
      </SetupThreadGroup>
      <hashTree>

        <!-- Push the draft: 4 options. multi/public come from variables. -->
        <HTTPSamplerProxy guiclass="HttpTestSampleGui" testclass="HTTPSamplerProxy"
                          testname="PUT host/poll/update (4-option draft)" enabled="true">
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.path">${HOST_POLL_BASE}/update</stringProp>
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.method">PUT</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.postBodyRaw">true</boolProp>
          <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments">
            <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
              <elementProp name="" elementType="HTTPArgument">
                <boolProp name="HTTPArgument.always_encode">false</boolProp>
                <stringProp name="Argument.value">{"question":"Load Test — pick an option","options":["Option A","Option B","Option C","Option D"],"multi":${MULTI},"public":true}</stringProp>
                <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
              </elementProp>
            </collectionProp>
          </elementProp>
        </HTTPSamplerProxy>
        <hashTree>
          <HeaderManager guiclass="HeaderPanel" testclass="HeaderManager"
                         testname="Content-Type: application/json" enabled="true">
            <collectionProp name="HeaderManager.headers">
              <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
                <stringProp name="Header.name">Content-Type</stringProp>
                <stringProp name="Header.value">application/json</stringProp>
              </elementProp>
            </collectionProp>
          </HeaderManager>
          <hashTree/>
          <ResponseAssertion guiclass="AssertionGui" testclass="ResponseAssertion"
                             testname="Assert 204" enabled="true">
            <collectionProp name="Asserion.test_strings">
              <stringProp name="51512">204</stringProp>
            </collectionProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.custom_message">Failed to push poll draft (host/poll/update)</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.test_field">Assertion.response_code</stringProp>
            <boolProp name="Assertion.assume_success">false</boolProp>
            <intProp name="Assertion.test_type">8</intProp>
          </ResponseAssertion>
          <hashTree/>
        </hashTree>

        <!-- Start the poll so participant votes are accepted -->
        <HTTPSamplerProxy guiclass="HttpTestSampleGui" testclass="HTTPSamplerProxy"
                          testname="POST host/poll/start" enabled="true">
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.path">${HOST_POLL_BASE}/start</stringProp>
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.method">POST</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.postBodyRaw">false</boolProp>
          <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments">
            <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments"/>
          </elementProp>
        </HTTPSamplerProxy>
        <hashTree>
          <ResponseAssertion guiclass="AssertionGui" testclass="ResponseAssertion"
                             testname="Assert 204" enabled="true">
            <collectionProp name="Asserion.test_strings">
              <stringProp name="51512">204</stringProp>
            </collectionProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.custom_message">Failed to start poll (host/poll/start)</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.test_field">Assertion.response_code</stringProp>
            <boolProp name="Assertion.assume_success">false</boolProp>
            <intProp name="Assertion.test_type">8</intProp>
          </ResponseAssertion>
          <hashTree/>
        </hashTree>

      </hashTree>

      <!-- ================================================================
           2. PARTICIPANTS: NUM_PARTICIPANTS threads each casting
              VOTES_PER_PARTICIPANT votes (random option, paced).
           ================================================================ -->
      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup"
                   testname="Participants (${NUM_PARTICIPANTS} threads)" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">continue</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController"
                     guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController">
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">false</boolProp>
          <stringProp name="LoopController.loops">${VOTES_PER_PARTICIPANT}</stringProp>
        </elementProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">${NUM_PARTICIPANTS}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">${RAMP_UP_SEC}</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">false</boolProp>
      </ThreadGroup>
      <hashTree>

        <!-- The vote request. X-Participant-ID identifies the (mutable) voter. -->
        <HTTPSamplerProxy guiclass="HttpTestSampleGui" testclass="HTTPSamplerProxy"
                          testname="POST poll/vote (random option)" enabled="true">
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.path">${VOTE_PATH}</stringProp>
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.method">POST</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.postBodyRaw">true</boolProp>
          <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments">
            <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
              <elementProp name="" elementType="HTTPArgument">
                <boolProp name="HTTPArgument.always_encode">false</boolProp>
                <stringProp name="Argument.value">{"options":[${__Random(0,${MAX_OPTION_INDEX},)}]}</stringProp>
                <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
              </elementProp>
            </collectionProp>
          </elementProp>
        </HTTPSamplerProxy>
        <hashTree>
          <!-- Identify the voter by thread number: ${__threadNum} is constant for a
               given thread across all its loop iterations (so re-votes update the SAME
               voter, exercising the mutable-vote path) and is unique across the group,
               giving exactly NUM_PARTICIPANTS distinct voters. Pure built-in function —
               no Groovy/JSR223, so it works under any Java (Groovy in JMeter 5.4.3 cannot
               compile on Java 17+). -->
          <HeaderManager guiclass="HeaderPanel" testclass="HeaderManager"
                         testname="Content-Type + X-Participant-ID" enabled="true">
            <collectionProp name="HeaderManager.headers">
              <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
                <stringProp name="Header.name">Content-Type</stringProp>
                <stringProp name="Header.value">application/json</stringProp>
              </elementProp>
              <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
                <stringProp name="Header.name">X-Participant-ID</stringProp>
                <stringProp name="Header.value">loadtest-p${__threadNum}</stringProp>
              </elementProp>
            </collectionProp>
          </HeaderManager>
          <hashTree/>
          <ResponseAssertion guiclass="AssertionGui" testclass="ResponseAssertion"
                             testname="Assert 204 (vote accepted)" enabled="true">
            <collectionProp name="Asserion.test_strings">
              <stringProp name="51512">204</stringProp>
            </collectionProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.custom_message">Vote rejected (409 = poll not active/invalid option; 400 = missing participant id)</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.test_field">Assertion.response_code</stringProp>
            <boolProp name="Assertion.assume_success">false</boolProp>
            <intProp name="Assertion.test_type">8</intProp>
          </ResponseAssertion>
          <hashTree/>
          <!-- Pace between a participant's successive (re-)votes -->
          <ConstantTimer guiclass="ConstantTimerGui" testclass="ConstantTimer"
                         testname="Pause between votes (${VOTE_INTERVAL_MS} ms)" enabled="true">
            <stringProp name="ConstantTimer.delay">${VOTE_INTERVAL_MS}</stringProp>
          </ConstantTimer>
          <hashTree/>
        </hashTree>

      </hashTree>

      <!-- ================================================================
           3. TEARDOWN: clear the poll
           ================================================================ -->
      <PostThreadGroup guiclass="PostThreadGroupGui" testclass="PostThreadGroup"
                       testname="Teardown: Clear Poll" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">continue</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController"
                     guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController">
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">false</boolProp>
          <stringProp name="LoopController.loops">1</stringProp>
        </elementProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">1</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">0</stringProp>
      </PostThreadGroup>
      <hashTree>
        <HTTPSamplerProxy guiclass="HttpTestSampleGui" testclass="HTTPSamplerProxy"
                          testname="POST host/poll/clear" enabled="true">
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.path">${HOST_POLL_BASE}/clear</stringProp>
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.method">POST</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.postBodyRaw">false</boolProp>
          <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments">
            <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments"/>
          </elementProp>
        </HTTPSamplerProxy>
        <hashTree/>
      </hashTree>

      <!-- ================================================================
           LISTENERS — Summary + Aggregate enabled; Results Tree off (heavy)
           ================================================================ -->
      <ResultCollector guiclass="ViewResultsFullVisualizer" testclass="ResultCollector"
                       testname="View Results Tree (debug — disabled)" enabled="false">
        <boolProp name="ResultCollector.error_logging">false</boolProp>
        <objProp>
          <name>saveConfig</name>
          <value class="SampleSaveConfiguration">
            <time>true</time><latency>true</latency><timestamp>true</timestamp><success>true</success>
            <label>true</label><code>true</code><message>true</message><threadName>true</threadName>
            <dataType>true</dataType><encoding>false</encoding><assertions>true</assertions>
            <subresults>true</subresults><responseData>false</responseData><samplerData>false</samplerData>
            <xml>false</xml><fieldNames>true</fieldNames><responseHeaders>false</responseHeaders>
            <requestHeaders>false</requestHeaders><responseDataOnError>true</responseDataOnError>
            <saveAssertionResultsFailureMessage>true</saveAssertionResultsFailureMessage>
            <bytes>true</bytes><sentBytes>true</sentBytes><url>true</url><threadCounts>true</threadCounts>
            <idleTime>true</idleTime><connectTime>true</connectTime>
          </value>
        </objProp>
        <stringProp name="filename"></stringProp>
      </ResultCollector>
      <hashTree/>

      <ResultCollector guiclass="SummaryReport" testclass="ResultCollector"
                       testname="Summary Report" enabled="true">
        <boolProp name="ResultCollector.error_logging">false</boolProp>
        <objProp>
          <name>saveConfig</name>
          <value class="SampleSaveConfiguration">
            <time>true</time><latency>true</latency><timestamp>true</timestamp><success>true</success>
            <label>true</label><code>true</code><message>true</message><threadName>true</threadName>
            <dataType>true</dataType><encoding>false</encoding><assertions>true</assertions>
            <subresults>true</subresults><responseData>false</responseData><samplerData>false</samplerData>
            <xml>false</xml><fieldNames>true</fieldNames><responseHeaders>false</responseHeaders>
            <requestHeaders>false</requestHeaders><responseDataOnError>false</responseDataOnError>
            <saveAssertionResultsFailureMessage>true</saveAssertionResultsFailureMessage>
            <bytes>true</bytes><sentBytes>true</sentBytes><url>true</url><threadCounts>true</threadCounts>
            <idleTime>true</idleTime><connectTime>true</connectTime>
          </value>
        </objProp>
        <stringProp name="filename"></stringProp>
      </ResultCollector>
      <hashTree/>

      <ResultCollector guiclass="StatVisualizer" testclass="ResultCollector"
                       testname="Aggregate Report (percentiles)" enabled="true">
        <boolProp name="ResultCollector.error_logging">false</boolProp>
        <objProp>
          <name>saveConfig</name>
          <value class="SampleSaveConfiguration">
            <time>true</time><latency>true</latency><timestamp>true</timestamp><success>true</success>
            <label>true</label><code>true</code><message>true</message><threadName>true</threadName>
            <dataType>true</dataType><encoding>false</encoding><assertions>true</assertions>
            <subresults>true</subresults><responseData>false</responseData><samplerData>false</samplerData>
            <xml>false</xml><fieldNames>true</fieldNames><responseHeaders>false</responseHeaders>
            <requestHeaders>false</requestHeaders><responseDataOnError>false</responseDataOnError>
            <saveAssertionResultsFailureMessage>true</saveAssertionResultsFailureMessage>
            <bytes>true</bytes><sentBytes>true</sentBytes><url>true</url><threadCounts>true</threadCounts>
            <idleTime>true</idleTime><connectTime>true</connectTime>
          </value>
        </objProp>
        <stringProp name="filename"></stringProp>
      </ResultCollector>
      <hashTree/>

    </hashTree>
  </hashTree>
</jmeterTestPlan>
